lesson: 105
title: The perimeter of a rectangle
stars: 0
explain: The perimeter is the distance all the way around a shape: add the lengths of all its sides.
explain: A rectangle has two long sides and two short sides: a rectangle 7 cm long and 3 cm wide has a perimeter of 7 + 3 + 7 + 3 = 20 cm.
explain: A square has four equal sides: a square with sides of 5 cm has a perimeter of 4 × 5 = 20 cm.
vars: a=name l=3..40 w=2..30
need: l > w
answer: 2 * (l + w)
exercise: A rectangle is {l} cm long and {w} cm wide. What is its perimeter in cm?
exercise: {a} walks all the way around a rectangular field {l} m long and {w} m wide. How many meters does {a.he} walk?
exercise: A rectangular garden is {l} m by {w} m. How many meters of fence go around it?
exercise: Find the perimeter of a rectangle with sides of {l} cm and {w} cm.
exercise: {a} puts ribbon around the edge of a rectangular card {l} cm long and {w} cm wide. How many cm of ribbon does {a.he} need?
exercise: A rectangular pool is {l} m long and {w} m wide. How far is it around the pool?
test: How many cm long is the border of a photo that measures {w} cm by {l} cm?
test: {a} runs once around a playground shaped like a rectangle, {w} m wide and {l} m long. What distance does {a.he} run?
test: The sides of a rectangular table are {l} dm and {w} dm. What is the total length of all four sides in dm?
test: A farmer fences a rectangular pen. Its width is {w} m and its length is {l} m. How many meters of fence does the farmer use?
exercise: What is the perimeter of a rectangle {w} cm wide and {l} cm long?
exercise: A rectangular yard in Georgia is {l} m long and {w} m wide. How many meters is it all the way around?
exercise: {a} in Leeds puts a border around a rectangular notice board {l} dm long and {w} dm wide. How many dm of border does {a.he} need?
exercise: A rectangle has a length of {l.words} cm and a width of {w.words} cm. Find the total length of its four sides in cm.
exercise: A rectangle is {l} m by {w} m. What is its perimeter in m?
exercise: How many meters of rope go once around a rectangular sandpit that measures {w} m by {l} m?
exercise: {a} jogs one lap around a rectangular park in Melbourne. The park is {l} m long and {w} m wide. How far does {a.he} jog in meters?
exercise: A rectangular window is {l} dm long and {w} dm wide. How many dm of frame go around it?
test: How many cm of lace go all around a rectangular tablecloth whose sides measure {l} cm and {w} cm?
test: A rugby pitch in Wellington is shaped like a rectangle, {l} m long and {w} m across. {a} walks once around its edge. How many meters is that?
test: The two short sides of a rectangle are {w} cm each and the two long sides are {l} cm each. What do all the sides add up to in cm?
test: Lights are hung along every edge of a rectangular stage {w} m deep and {l} m wide. How many meters of lights are used?
test: A rectangular map of Ireland is {l} cm by {w} cm. What length of tape goes once around its edge, in cm?
test: In Arizona, {a} builds a rectangular pen {w} m wide and {l} m long. How many meters of wire make one loop around it?
