exam: It is given that a rectangle has a length of {l} cm and a width of {w} cm. Determine its perimeter, expressed in centimetres.
exam: Ascertain the distance, in metres, traversed by {a} in walking once around the boundary of a rectangular field measuring {l} m by {w} m.
exam: Whereas a rectangular plot is {l} metres in length and {w} metres in breadth, state the length of fencing, in metres, required to enclose it entirely.
exam: Compute the sum of the lengths of all four sides of a rectangle whose dimensions are {l} cm and {w} cm.
exercise: The memorial garden where Grandpa was laid to rest is a rectangle {l} m long and {w} m wide. How many meters of edging go all the way around it?
exercise: The estate agent calls the yard "bijou": it is only {l} m long and {w} m wide. How many meters of fence go all the way around it?
